# Confidential realtime feed

## Never expose

- Vendor/product names (e.g. Pulsar, Apache Pulsar, TRAC, pulsarplatform)
- Upstream GraphQL URL or any provider hostname
- Access tokens, bearer headers, search hashes, broker/topic/queue names
- Raw GraphQL queries, GraphQL errors, stack traces, or upstream response bodies
- Debug logs of API payloads in the browser (`console.log` / `warn` / `info` / `debug` / unnecessary `error`)

## Required architecture

- Browser talks only to first-party routes (e.g. `/api/signals-feed`)
- Upstream URL + credentials live in **server-only** env (`FEED_UPSTREAM_URL`, `FEED_API_TOKEN`, `FEED_SEARCH_HASH`) — never `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`
- On failure: return empty/safe data; do not send technical error strings to the client
- UI copy stays product-facing (e.g. “Live signal”) — never infrastructure language

## Production bar

- No debug components, homepage probes, or developer-only overlays for this feed
- Client catch blocks stay silent; no toast/banner that reveals internals
